Generate 0037-lus-gui-3d-menu-split.patch.

The 3D stereo path (0034) renders both eyes offscreen and NEVER runs the
normal gui StartDraw/EndDraw (that path acquires the hidden window's
drawable and draws the 2D game viewport). So on the panel the LUS menu and
the perf HUD are invisible. Split the frame:

  * Soh3DBuildMenuFrame() — run the ImGui frame WITHOUT the backend
    NewFrame (the 0034 loop primed ImGui_ImplMetal against an eye
    framebuffer) and WITHOUT the Main-Deck dockspace / DrawGame (that
    hosts the game image and its window size drives CalculateGameViewport
    = the top-left crop trap the Ship of Harkinian port hit). Draw the modern menu
    (GetMenu, the PortMenu) + menubar directly, transparent, plus the
    perf HUD into the foreground draw list (rides in the draw data, so it
    reaches both eyes).
  * Soh3DGetDrawData() — hand the built ImDrawData to the 0034 loop, which
    renders it into BOTH eye framebuffers (flat on the panel).
  * Soh3DFinishMenuFrame() — EndFrame + CheckSaveCvars once per host frame.

Starship divergence vs the SpaghettiKart 0043 template: SpaghettiKart's
live menu is SpaghettiGui::DrawMenu (a Gui subclass override) and the
split calls DrawMenu() wholesale. Starship's menu is the modern PortMenu
registered via Gui::SetMenu and drawn by GetMenu()->Draw(); there is no
game Gui subclass. So this build method draws GetMenu()/GetMenuBar()
DIRECTLY and never touches the Main-Deck dockspace — the "Main Game"
re-dock self-heal SpaghettiKart needed is unnecessary here (3D never docks
Main Game). The menu lays out against WorkSize, which imgui derives from
io.DisplaySize; we override that to a 1920x1080 logical canvas (the parked
window is only 480x320 = an 8x-too-large menu on the panel). The render
step's FramebufferScale recompute (0034) maps it onto the eye texture.

Depends on the 0034 shell externs + Soh3DImGuiPrime/Render and the shell's
SohIos_PerfHud3DText (SohVision3D.m). __IOS__-guarded: the macOS build
compiles this overlaid vendor but never references these (its caller in
Fast3dWindow is __IOS__-guarded too).


